KG42.register("rules-f9353ff969429387868a965a",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R012","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R012","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Energy-trade execution","process_stage":"activation","market_meaning":"The same local market clearing price applies to the trades executed by all winning participants. Scope: Uniform k-DA in the local energy market. Condition: Participants are auction winners.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function execution.energy_trade under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R012-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R012-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Uniform k-DA in the local energy market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R012-T-k","symbol":"k","meaning":"Constant weight k in the Uniform k-DA market-clearing price kB_\\gamma^P + (1-k)S_\\gamma^P; it weights the marginal bid price B_\\gamma^P with complementary weight (1-k) on the marginal ask price S_\\gamma^P. Scope: Uniform k-DA in the local energy market (same-mechanism constant of v141-a-M02).","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"k"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R012-T-Bgamma","symbol":"B_{\\gamma}^{P}","meaning":"Bid price at the largest breakeven index \\gamma (B_\\gamma^P), used as the marginal bid in the Uniform k-DA market-clearing price. Treated as a fixed input at the execution/activation stage of this rule (it is determined by the preceding clearing). Scope: Uniform k-DA in the local energy market.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"B_{\\gamma}^{P}"},"unit":null,"indices":["\\gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R012-T-Sgamma","symbol":"S_{\\gamma}^{P}","meaning":"Ask price at the largest breakeven index \\gamma (S_\\gamma^P), used as the marginal ask in the Uniform k-DA market-clearing price. Treated as a fixed input at the execution/activation stage of this rule (it is determined by the preceding clearing). Scope: Uniform k-DA in the local energy market.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"S_{\\gamma}^{P}"},"unit":null,"indices":["\\gamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The same local market clearing price applies to the trades executed by all winning participants. Scope: Uniform k-DA in the local energy market. Condition: Participants are auction winners.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Under Uniform k-DA, all winning participants trade at the same market clearing price: both the price trading buyers pay and the price trading sellers receive equal kB_\\gamma^P + (1-k)S_\\gamma^P, the single-unit-auction price formed at the largest breakeven index \\gamma, where B_\\gamma^P and S_\\gamma^P are the bid and ask prices at that index and k is the mechanism constant. Scope: Uniform k-DA in the local energy market. Condition: participants are auction winners.","expression":"p^{*} = k B_{\\gamma}^{P} + (1 - k) S_{\\gamma}^{P}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R012-T-k","v141-c-R012-T-Bgamma","v141-c-R012-T-Sgamma"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-04"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-02","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminatory k-DA where all winning participants trade at the same price. Such market clearing price is figured by first sorting offers according to the natural ordering rule and determining the largest breakeven index $\\gamma$ where $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$. The market clearing price is then calculated as for single-unit auctions where $B_{\\gamma}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma}^P$ are the bid and ask prices at the largest breakeven index, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-04","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Table 1 Auction mechanisms. Uniform k-DA | Price trading buyers pay: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$ | Price trading sellers receive: $kB_{\\gamma}^P + (1 - k)S_{\\gamma}^P$"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"This activation/execution rule exposes no design-selection or operational decision variable: it states a property of the Uniform k-DA clearing price as applied to already-won trades. The constituent symbols (k, B_\\gamma^P, S_\\gamma^P) are determined by the preceding clearing stage and are therefore modeled as fixed inputs (theta), not as decision variables.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-clearing","v141-a-M02-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-02","quote":"Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminatory k-DA where all winning participants trade at the same price."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"0809b002a06f37d22a110db9b97d8340c213e53a87f81497fa933c6fde965e64","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The frozen rule links pricing.local to execution.energy_trade for Uniform k-DA (v141-a-M02). Candidate same-mechanism evidence v141-b-g01-ev-04 (Table 1) gives the uniform trading price kB_\\gamma^P + (1-k)S_\\gamma^P paid by buyers and received by sellers, and v141-b-g01-ev-02 states that all winning participants trade at the same market clearing price at the largest breakeven index. This supports the added supporting mathematical constraint C002 (uniform price applied to executed trades of all winners). The existing core procedural constraint C001 is preserved unchanged. The graph already represents the pricing->execution relationship (edge v141-c-R012-E001), so no graph revision is required. All quoted evidence here is UNREVIEWED candidate support (source_status unverified); this output does not assert verified source correctness.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-T-k","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"k is a constant of the pricing.local entity: it parameterizes the single Uniform k-DA clearing price that pricing.local supplies to execution.energy_trade."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-T-Bgamma","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The marginal bid price B_\\gamma^P is an input to the Uniform k-DA clearing price held in pricing.local; it is fixed before execution and feeds the price that links to execution.energy_trade."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-T-Sgamma","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The marginal ask price S_\\gamma^P is an input to the Uniform k-DA clearing price held in pricing.local; it is fixed before execution and feeds the price that links to execution.energy_trade."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","node_ids":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R012-E001"],"rationale":"C002 states that the single clearing price determined at pricing.local is the same price applied to the trades executed in execution.energy_trade, i.e. the uniform price is what the frozen edge v141-c-R012-E001 (pricing.local -> execution.energy_trade, type 'links') expresses."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
